# Pull requests

- The title is a Conventional Commits line (`.cursor/rules/conventional-commits.mdc`). Its type is the kind of the row the PR finishes.
- The body uses the six headings of `.github/pull_request_template.md`, in order, in English: `## Summary`, `## Related`, `## Test plan`, `## Verification`, `## Risk / Rollback`, `## Checklist`. List text under them may be Japanese. An empty section is `N/A`. Do not invent headings.
- Start a body from the template file, not from an earlier PR's body.
- An acceptance line the PR cannot fill means the PR does not finish that Issue: write `Part of #N`, not `Closes #N` (`.cursor/rules/github-closing.mdc`).
- `## Verification` has, before anything else, every line of the Issue's Definition of done with what met it, or "not met" and where it went. It is written before `gh pr create`, from the Issue as it reads then, not from memory. #137, #139, and #140 each closed an Issue with a line unmet, one after the other, with the rule above already in this file: the lines were not laid next to the work until a review did it.
- A hot-path PR pastes the criterion comparison against the named baseline under `## Verification`, or says why speed does not change (`.cursor/rules/bench.mdc`).
- A statement that "the output is unchanged" names its grain: bit for bit, or equal within a stated tolerance.
- A PR stacked on another is merged into `main` only: when the PR under it merges, its base is `main` before anyone merges it. #167 was merged four minutes after the PR under it, into that PR's branch, which `main` no longer followed; it was reported as merged and was not on `main` (#166 carried it there). After a merge, `git log origin/main` has the commit, or the merge did not happen.
- Read the body again when its base merges and when a commit lands after it was written. A "Stacked on #N" line is rewritten once #N merges.
- Edit a body from a UTF-8 file with `--body-file`, check it is not empty, and read it back.
- Of two PRs open side by side, only the one that merges later edits the Current work line of `docs/roadmap.md`, after taking `main` in (a merge, not a rebase). #175 and #177 both rewrote it and the line beside it, and #177 conflicted.
